    "title": "Columbia County Democrat leader on Commission District 4 blue shift - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Lynch ,\n5 hours ago\nEVANS Ga (WJBF) - A shakeup on the Columbia County Board of Commissioners. The county that is usually red now has a little blue.\nDemocrat Samantha Rockwood beat Republican Al Reaves in a close race for the District 4 seat. Rockwood replaces Alison Couch who is now the Commission Chair Elect.\nRockwood is the first democrat on the commission for as long as many people can remember.\n\"The last I recall might have been in the 80's when there was a lot of political realignment happening,\" said Chairman of the Columbia County Democratic Party Parin Amin. \"So it's been, you know, at least my lifetime.\"\nParin said people in the county wanted changed. He said he hopes it will lead to improved transparency for voters.\nNewsChannel6 reached out to Samantha Rockwood but she was unavailable.\nColumbia County Elections Director Nancy Gay said voter turnout was among the top 25 in Georgia.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJBF.\nAdd to Preferred Sources",
